diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..7f6d44a 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,16 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string or null>}`: one page
+  of items, ordered by `id`.
+  - `limit` (optional): an integer from 1 to 100. Defaults to 20.
+  - `cursor` (optional): the `next_cursor` from a previous response. Pass it back
+    unchanged; treat it as opaque.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. To read everything, request the
+    first page with no cursor, then keep passing `next_cursor` until it is `null`.
+  - An invalid `limit` or `cursor` gets 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
+  - Breaking change: `GET /items` without `limit` now returns only the first 20
+    items. Callers that need everything must follow `next_cursor`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
